    "Business Courses in English\nBusiness Courses in English\nWe offer numerous business courses taught in English that are open to exchange students enrolled at the School of Business.\nYou can take courses covering a wide variety of topics; some require prior knowledge.\nFor all of the courses listed below, you must demonstrate at least a B2 level of English proficiency.\nBusiness Courses for Exchange Students (School of Business) - Undergraduate\nStudy Focus' for Bachelor's Exchange Students\nElective Courses for Bachelor's and Master's Programs (School of Business)\nBusiness Courses for Master's Exchange Students (School of Business) - Graduate\nAdditional Electives\nBusiness Courses for Exchange Students (School of Business) - Undergraduate\nThe following bachelor's-level courses are part of the \"International Management\" (IM) degree program and are open to exchange students.\nCode\nCourse Title\nSemester\nSWS\nECTS\nTerm\n2845939\nFundamentals in Business\n1\n4\n5\nWinter\n2845942\nMultinational Business Finance and Investment\n3\n4\n5\nWinter\n2845943\nInternational Economics\n3\n4\n5\nWinter\n2845941\nHuman Resource and Organizational Management\n3\n4\n5\nWinter\n2840060\nEconomics 1\n2\n4\n5\nSummer\n2845923\nFinancing and Capital Markets\n2\n4\n5\nSummer\n2845941\nHuman Resource and Organizational Management\n4\n4\n3\nSummer\n2845921\nControlling\n4\n4\n5\nSummer\n2845924\nScientific Methodology (Research Methods in Finance)\n4\n4\n5\nSummer\n2845922\nCross-Cultural Management\n4\n4\n5\nSummer\n2845955\nProduction & Logistics\n4\n4\n5\nSummer\n2845975\nInternational Sales Law\n4\n4\n5\nSummer\n2842125\nIntermediate Business English\n3.+\n4\n5\nWinter/Summer\n2842126\nAdvanced Business English (Oral)\n3.+\n4\n5\nWinter/Summer\n2842127\nAdvanced Business English (Written)\n3.+\n4\n5\nWinter/Summer\n2845967\nApplied Business Management\n6/7\n2\n2\nWinter/Summer\n2845947\nStrategic Management and Simulation\n6/7\n4\n5\nWinter/Summer\nStudy Focus' for Bachelor's Exchange Students\nEach study focus consists of several modules totaling 12 ECTS. Students may take only one specialization per semester.\nPrior knowledge is required for the Marketing specialization.\nCode\nCourse Title\nSemester\nSWS\nECTS\nTerm\nPrerequisites\n2845944\nHuman Resources\n5\n6\n9\nWinter\n2845945\nLogistics and Supply Chain Management\n5\n8\n12\nWinter\n2844103\nAccounting and Taxation\n5\n8\n12\nWinter\n2845978\nCorporate Finance & Capital Markets\n6\n8\n12\nSummer\n2845985\nManaging Data-Driven Business Models\n6\n8\n12\nSummer\n2845911\nInternational Marketing\n6\n8\n12\nSummer\nPrerequisite Knowledge\n(to be verified by transcript)\nElective Courses for Bachelor's and Master's Programs (School of Business)\nThe School of Business offers a variety of elective courses that exchange students can take.\nCode\nCourse Title\nSemester\nSWS\nECTS\nTerm\n2845938\nLean Management\n4/5\n2\n3\nWinter\n2845922\nCross-Cultural Management (for exchange students only)\n4/5\n4\n5\nWinter\n2846008\nEnvironmental Economics and Climate Change\n4/5\n4\n4\nWinter/Summer\n2846016\nEuropean Integration\n4/5\n4\n4\nSummer\nBusiness Courses for Master's Exchange Students (School of Business) - Graduate\nThese master's-level courses are part of the \"International Business and Finance\" (IBF) degree program and are generally open only to master's students.\nBachelor's students should contact the IFCs!\nCode\nCourse Title\nSemester\nSWS\nECTS\nTerm\nPrerequisite\n(verified by transcript)\n9410020\nBusiness Ethics and Corporate Governance\n1\n4\n6\nWinter\n-\n2845950\nFinancial Economics, Financial Institutions, and Monetary Policy\n1\n4\n6\nWinter\nBasic knowledge of economics\n2845948\nFinancial Market Decisions\n1\n4\n6\nWinter\nBasic Knowledge of Finance\n2845949\nManaging People\n1\n4\n6\nWinter\nBasic Knowledge of Human Resource Management\n2845951\nValuation of Securities and Companies\n1\n4\n6\nWinter\nIn-Depth Knowledge of Corporate Finance\n9610120\nPlatform & Digital Design Strategies\n2\n4\n6\nSummer\nBasic Knowledge of Strategic Management\n2846011\nCorporate Finance & Valuation\n2\n4\n6\nSummer\nAdvanced knowledge of finance\n9610080\nBanking Regulations & Supervision\n2\n4\n6\nSummer\nIn-depth knowledge of finance\n9410160\nStrategy Case Study - Simulation\n2\n4\n6\nSummer\nIn-depth knowledge of strategic management\n9410170\nInternational Guest Lecture\n2\n4\n6\nSummer\nIn-depth knowledge of finance\n9410082\nAdvanced Risk Management\n3\n2\n4\nWinter\nIn-depth knowledge of finance\n9610300\nAdvanced M&A Management\n3\n2\n4\nWinter\nIn-depth knowledge of finance\n9610310\nAdvanced M&A Management - Valuation & Case Studies\n3\n2\n4\nWinter\nIn-depth knowledge of finance\nAdditional Electives\nThe Center for Languages and Intercultural Communication (ZSI) offers many other elective courses university-wide.\nAmong others, students can also enroll in the following courses:\nCode\nCourse Title\nSWS\nECTS\nWinter/Summer\n9905560\nStudying and Living in Germany\n2\n2\nWinter/Summer\n9905460\nIntercultural Competence—A Key Professional Competence\n2\n2\nWinter/Summer\nCenter for Languages (ZSI)"
